  "worked_solution": "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{B}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{B(t)-B(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{\u2032}(6) & \u2248\\frac{B(6)-B(6-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{B(6)-B(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-55}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the estimated rate of change when $t=6$ is $-\\frac{15}{2}$ percent per hour.",
